      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think it would be more straight forward/useful to replace the system_rollback_detected check with a board_id_mismatched check.\n \nIn terms of the old cr50 behavior I dont think the rollback check is useful, but with that weird board id rollback state the check is. This system_rollback_detected check prevents us from setting the state to UNLOCKED when we have rolled back to a board id mismatched image. When we are in that state we dont try to jump to the other image, and we just continue booting in a locked down state, so I think ccd should not be set to UNLOCKED in that state.\n\nI assume that there will be a better check somewhere else to make sure that even if the system is UNLOCKED then nothing ccd related will actually be unlocked if there is a mismatch.\n\nSo I am not sure if you want to prevent the unlock here or not. Maybe ccd_get_state would be a good place... just always return locked if the board id is mismatched",
